act is limited to that quote, so the wider survey of views is not covered here.", "hook": "Former Seventh Circuit judge Diane Wood says AI judge profiles are already out of control and cannot be stopped.", "entities": ["Legal Tech Monitor", "Diane Wood", "U.S. Court of Appeals for the Seventh Circuit"], "jurisdiction": null, "amount": null, "provenance": "independently-reported", "status": "live", "story_type": "analysis", "deal_kind": null, "adoption_kind": null, "rule_kind": null, "adoption_claim": null, "ai_lens": "AI.PRA", "ai": true, "topic": "courts-and-justice", "taxonomy_version": "3.2", "scope": "legal-it", "taxonomy_only": null}, {"id": "LN-20261122-009", "cluster_id": "LN-20261122-009", "register_day": "2026-11-22", "first_seen": "2026-11-21T21:57:04+00:00", "published_at": "2026-11-20T05:38:40+00:00", "title": "Three Questions Every Firm Should Ask Before Its Next AI Investment", "url": "https://legaltechmonitor.com/2026/11/three-questions-every-firm-should-ask-before-its-next-ai-investment", "domain": "legaltechmonitor.com", "source_name": "Legal Tech Monitor", "source_kind": "aggregator", "seen_in": [{"source_name": "Legal Tech Monitor", "url": "https://legaltechmonitor.com/2026/11/three-questions-every-firm-should-ask-before-its-next-ai-investment"}], "category": "finance-pms", "region": "us", "market": "US", "language": "en", "kind": "news-report", "paywall": false, "ltme_summary": "Legal Tech Monitor sets out a view that firm profit depends on how AI-enabled work moves through the whole economic chain, not only on how fast lawyers work. The piece names matters, pricing, realisation, billing and collections as the stages firms need visibility over. It is an opinion piece, and the author and any vendor link are not shown in the extract.", "hook": "Legal Tech Monitor argues firms must track AI work across matters, pricing, billing and collections to make profit.", "entities": ["Legal Tech Monitor"], "jurisdiction": null, "amount": null, "provenance": "